    "description": "Job Title: Smart Office & Administration Coordinator Company: Organic Liquid Fertilizer Producing P.L.C. (Brand: ECO GREEN) Location: Addis Ababa, Ethiopia Employment Type: Full-time Salary: Competitive (based on experience) Application Deadline: 30 November 2026 We are looking for a technology-driven professional who can help EcoGreen transition from manual operations to a fully integrated digital workspace. BUILD A SMARTER, FASTER, MORE PROFESSIONAL OFFICE Organic Liquid Fertilizer Producing P.L.C., operating under the brand name ECO GREEN, is transforming into a modern, system-driven organization. We are looking for a highly capable, digitally skilled, and proactive Smart Office & Administration Coordinator who can help us build an efficient, organized, and accountable working environment. This is not a traditional office administration position. We are specifically looking for candidates who have transitioned beyond manual filing and can demonstrate hands-on experience working in a smart, digitally integrated office environment. The right candidate should understand how modern organizations use digital technology, ERP systems, and integrated workflows to manage information, coordinate activities, monitor responsibilities, and improve operational efficiency. 1. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES A. Smart Office & Digital Operations - Coordinate daily office operations using digital tools and structured workflows. - Maintain an organized, efficient, and technology-enabled working environment. - Coordinate office resources, facilities, appointments, services, and official activities. - Identify opportunities to reduce manual work and improve operational efficiency. B. ERP & Business Systems - Use the company's ERP and other digital platforms for administrative coordination and information management. - Ensure administrative activities and records are properly managed through digital systems. - Support employees in following established digital processes. - Monitor system-based administrative tasks and ensure timely completion. C. Digital Workflow & Accountability - Track management decisions, assigned tasks, deadlines, and pending commitments using digital tools. - Follow up with responsible employees and ensure actions are completed on time. - Identify delays, missing information, and unresolved issues and escalate them appropriately. - Maintain accurate and accessible digital action records. D. Executive & Management Coordination - Organize meetings, appointments, agendas, and management activities. - Prepare meeting minutes, action lists, and digital follow-up records. - Ensure management receives accurate and timely information. - Coordinate communication between management, departments, and company locations. E. Digital Document & Information Management - Manage electronic records, document control, shared digital workspaces, and structured filing systems. - Ensure company information is accurate, secure, accessible, and properly organized. - Manage official correspondence and confidential documents professionally. - Maintain reliable systems for document tracking and retrieval. F. Process Improvement - Develop and improve digital checklists, workflows, trackers, and administrative procedures. - Identify recurring administrative problems and recommend practical solutions. - Support the transition from informal and manual working practices to structured, system-based operations. - Contribute to building a professional, accountable, and efficient smart office. 2. MANDATORY PRACTICAL EXPERIENCE The successful candidate must demonstrate hands-on experience in: - Smart office management and digital office operations. - ERP or integrated business management software. - Digital task and workflow management. - Electronic document management and shared digital workspaces. - Digital meeting coordination and management action tracking. - Process improvement and reducing manual administrative work.",
