    "description": "Invitation for Consultancy Service About the Assignment The Civil Society Resource Center (CSRC) is an Ethiopian civil society support organization based in Addis Ababa. CSRC is a co-applicant, together with the Ethiopian Civil Society Organizations Forum (ECSF) and the Chura Abugida Artistic Association (CAAA), on the EU Civil Society Fund Plus (EU CSF Plus) Programme — a four-year action financed by the European Union and implemented by Christian Aid. The Programme operates in Tigray, South Ethiopia, Central Ethiopia and Addis Ababa City Administration, and provides sub-grants together with sustained capacity strengthening to sixty civil society organizations (CSOs). Under the Programme, CSRC is developing a shared library of training manuals that respond directly to the capacity gaps identified through organizational capacity assessments conducted across all four regions. CSRC invites qualified and licensed consultancy firms, or individual consultants, to submit technical and financial proposals for the development of training manuals, facilitator guides and delivery of training under the lots described below. Each lot corresponds to one term of reference. A bidder should submit for one lot only, and each lot is evaluated and contracted independently. Lots Open for Bidding Lot 1 — Governance, Human Resources and Organizational Systems : One integrated training manual covering : Module 1: Governance and Board Oversight — to enable boards and senior management to exercise effective oversight, apply governance policies in practice, and maintain current strategic plans. Module 2: Human Resource Management and Institutional Systems — to establish compliant recruitment, personnel records, induction and performance management systems. Module 3: Information Technology Systems and Data Protection — to put in place an information technology policy, secure data storage and backup, and responsible data handling practice across the organization. Module 4: Security and Risk Management — to develop security management plans and standard operating procedures, establish organizational risk registers, and build staff awareness of security procedures. Please see the detailed ToR here : https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X1pNoVfSXXv-BhU-LLya_kusJp9x0Rav/edit Lot 2 — Financial Management, Control and Compliance : One integrated training manual covering: Module 1: Financial Capacity and Adaptive Budgeting — to strengthen financial planning, budgeting and asset management so that resources are tracked and reported accurately across multiple donors. Module 2: Financial Control and Compliance — to establish internal controls, segregation of duties, procurement and payroll compliance, and the policy set required by donors and by regulators. Please see the detailed ToR here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Khv0T1AsEeNNnbriBUpS8FirZNqiw64A/edit Lot 3 — Safeguarding, Accountability, MEAL and Programme Quality : One integrated training manual covering: Module 1: Safeguarding, Accountability and Community Feedback — to move safeguarding and accountability from policy to practice through assigned focal points, functioning feedback and complaints mechanisms, and clear response procedures. Module 2: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Learning — to institutionalize monitoring systems that generate usable evidence and inform decision making. Module 3: Gender Equality and Social Inclusion — to embed gender and inclusion across governance structures, programming and organizational practice. Module 4: Programme Quality and Programme Cycle Management — to institutionalize programme cycle processes and quality standards so that delivery is consistent rather than project by project. Please see the detailed ToR here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WQd2cH7vM_nGyfrSkGo72qSJqjokrdP_/edit Lot 4 — Evidence-Based Policy Analysis, Advocacy and Communication : One integrated training manual covering: Module 1: Evidence-Based Policy Analysis and Advocacy — to build capacity to generate and analyse evidence, develop an organizational advocacy strategy, and engage credibly in policy dialogue at local, regional and federal level. Module 2: Stakeholder, Power and Context Analysis — to equip programme staff to map stakeholders and power relations and to conduct periodic context analysis that informs both programming and advocacy. Module 3: Media Engagement and Public Communication — to enable organizations to engage media and communicate positions publicly in support of advocacy objectives. Please see the detailed ToR here: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bdrYQCn-F9PAWWROnMvpmMESPO9R_5EI/edit Each lot is contracted as a single lump-sum consultancy against its own terms of reference. A bidder should submit for one lot only. Complete terms of reference, in English, are shared independently for the lot applied for",
