    "datePosted": "2026-11-15T17:14:41.000Z",
    "description": "Position Overview / Scope of Role The KIZEN & Operating Procedure Expert is responsible for leading and coordinating the implementation of the company's KIZEN (Kaizen) system, operational improvement initiatives, and standard operating procedures across departments. The role focuses on promoting a culture of continuous improvement, improving operational efficiency, eliminating process waste, standardizing work methods, strengthening process controls, and enhancing organizational productivity. The Expert works closely with department heads and employees to identify operational gaps, develop practical improvement solutions, establish performance monitoring mechanisms, and ensure that approved improvements are effectively implemented and sustained. The position also supports the development and maintenance of the company's management system documentation, including policies, procedures, work instructions, and relevant ISO 9001:2015 quality management system requirements. Top Roles and Responsibilities KIZEN System Development and Implementation Lead the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of the company's KIZEN system across all departments. Develop annual KIZEN implementation plans, departmental improvement targets, and implementation schedules aligned with company objectives. Establish structured mechanisms for identifying, evaluating, prioritizing, and implementing improvement opportunities. Promote KIZEN principles and continuous improvement practices as part of the company's organizational culture. Coordinate with department heads to ensure that KIZEN activities are integrated into daily operations and departmental work plans. Monitor the implementation of approved improvement initiatives and ensure their sustainability. Process Analysis and Operational Improvement Review existing operational processes, workflows, and working methods to identify inefficiencies, bottlenecks, duplication, and unnecessary activities. Identify and address the seven types of operational waste (Muda) through practical process improvement initiatives. Apply Kaizen, Lean Management, 5S, and other relevant continuous improvement methodologies. Conduct process assessments and recommend improvements to enhance productivity, quality, resource utilization, and cost efficiency. Facilitate root cause analysis of operational problems and coordinate the development and implementation of corrective and preventive action plans. Evaluate the effectiveness of implemented improvements and recommend further actions where necessary. Standard Operating Procedures and Process Standardization Develop, review, update, and maintain Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), work instructions, process guidelines, and operational manuals in coordination with relevant departments. Ensure that departmental procedures clearly define responsibilities, process steps, controls, and expected operational standards. Identify undocumented or inconsistently applied processes and facilitate their formalization and standardization. Ensure that approved procedures are communicated, accessible, and consistently applied across the organization. Review existing procedures periodically to ensure their relevance, effectiveness, and alignment with actual operational practices. Promote the sharing and replication of successful improvement practices across departments. ISO Management System and Document Control Support the development, implementation, maintenance, and continuous improvement of the company's ISO 9001:2015 Quality Management System. Coordinate the preparation and review of quality management system documentation, including policies, procedures, manuals, forms, and records. Establish and maintain effective document control practices to ensure proper approval, distribution, revision, accessibility, and retention of controlled documents. Coordinate internal process assessments and support the preparation and follow-up of audit findings and corrective actions. Monitor departmental compliance with approved procedures and relevant management system requirements. Coordinate with relevant departments to address nonconformities and improve the effectiveness of the management system. Performance Monitoring and Reporting Develop and monitor KIZEN-related KPIs and operational performance indicators in collaboration with relevant department heads. Establish mechanisms for measuring the results and impact of process improvement initiatives. Monitor improvement project progress, productivity gains, waste reduction, cost savings, and other operational efficiency indicators. Conduct regular 5S assessments and process compliance reviews. Prepare monthly KIZEN performance reports highlighting achievements, gaps, implementation progress, and recommended actions. Develop and maintain a continuous improvement performance dashboard for management review. Present improvement results, operational challenges, and recommendations to the General Manager and relevant management teams. Training, Coaching, and Employee Engagement Develop and deliver KIZEN awareness and training programs for employees, supervisors, and department heads. Facilitate workshops, improvement meetings, problem-solving sessions, and employee engagement activities. Coach employees and departmental teams on practical application of Kaizen, Lean, 5S, and problem-solving techniques. Encourage employee participation in identifying workplace problems and proposing improvement ideas. Promote teamwork, accountability, ownership, and a continuous improvement mindset throughout the organization. Recognize and communicate successful improvement initiatives to encourage wider participation. Cross-Functional Coordination and Improvement Projects Coordinate with department heads and process owners to identify and prioritize improvement projects. Facilitate cross-functional improvement teams and monitor the implementation of agreed action plans. Provide technical guidance and support to departments in process mapping, workflow analysis, and improvement project execution. Follow up on outstanding improvement actions and escalate implementation challenges to the General Manager. Ensure that improvement initiatives are practical, measurable, cost-effective, and aligned with company priorities. Documentation and Management Reporting Maintain records of KIZEN activities, improvement projects, audit results, training activities, and implementation progress. Prepare the annual KIZEN implementation plan, departmental improvement action plans, and monthly performance reports. Maintain an organized database of approved SOPs, work instructions, process improvement records, and related management system documents. Ensure timely submission of reports and management updates on KIZEN implementation and operational improvement performance. Performs other related duties as directed.",
