    "datePosted": "2026-11-15T17:00:03.000Z",
    "description": "Position Overview / Scope of Role The Quality Assurance Supervisor is responsible for supervising and ensuring the implementation of quality standards throughout the company's printing and manufacturing operations, from incoming raw materials and prepress activities through printing, finishing, packaging, and final product inspection. The position ensures that products conform to approved technical specifications, customer requirements, internal quality standards, and applicable regulatory requirements. The role supervises the QA/QC team, monitors production quality, identifies defects and process deviations, coordinates corrective and preventive actions, and works closely with Production, Prepress, Procurement, Warehouse, and Customer Service teams to maintain product consistency, minimize quality-related losses, and continuously improve operational performance. Top Roles and Responsibilities Quality Control and Inspection Supervise and coordinate quality inspections throughout the entire printing and production process. Establish, implement, and maintain quality inspection procedures, standards, checklists, and quality control checkpoints. Inspect incoming raw materials, including paper, paperboard, inks, coatings, adhesives, chemicals, and other printing consumables, to ensure compliance with approved specifications. Monitor product quality at different production stages, including prepress, printing, finishing, packaging, and final inspection. Ensure that printed products meet required specifications in terms of color accuracy, registration, image quality, text, dimensions, finishing, and overall appearance. Ensure non-conforming materials and products are properly identified, segregated, documented, and controlled. Review inspection results and recommend product acceptance, rejection, or reprocessing in accordance with established quality procedures and delegated authority. Ensure that quality inspections are conducted consistently and that identified defects are addressed promptly. Printing Process Quality Management Monitor and control quality parameters across applicable printing processes, including offset, digital, flexographic, gravure, and other printing technologies used by the company. Work closely with production personnel to identify, investigate, and prevent common printing and finishing defects, including color variations, poor registration, ink-related defects, misprinting, coating and varnishing defects, cutting and creasing problems, folding and binding errors, lamination defects, and incorrect or missing printed information. Ensure that production parameters and quality requirements are properly controlled and documented. Participate in machine setup inspections, press approvals, first-run inspections, and production start-up quality assessments. Monitor quality consistency during production runs and ensure that corrective actions are taken whenever deviations occur. Coordinate with Production and Prepress teams to ensure that approved artwork, printing specifications, and customer requirements are properly followed. Identify recurring production quality problems and recommend appropriate process adjustments and improvements. Quality Documentation and Reporting Maintain accurate quality inspection reports, checklists, testing records, product approval documents, and defect registers. Prepare and submit daily, weekly, and monthly quality performance reports. Monitor quality performance indicators, including rejection rates, rework, material wastage, internal defects, and customer complaints. Maintain records of non-conformities, corrective and preventive actions, and quality improvement activities. Ensure proper traceability of inspected materials, work-in-progress, and released finished products. Analyze quality performance trends and provide recommendations to management for improving product quality and reducing quality-related losses. Ensure that quality documentation is properly maintained and readily available for internal and external audits. Non-Conformance Management and Corrective Actions Identify, document, investigate, and report quality deviations and non-conforming products throughout the production process. Investigate internal quality failures and customer complaints in coordination with relevant departments. Conduct root-cause analysis using appropriate problem-solving techniques to identify the underlying causes of recurring quality problems. Coordinate the development and implementation of corrective and preventive actions with Production, Prepress, Procurement, and other relevant departments. Monitor the implementation and effectiveness of corrective and preventive actions. Recommend appropriate measures to prevent recurring defects, reduce rework, and improve production quality. Ensure that non-conforming products are properly controlled and not released without the required authorization. Team Supervision and Performance Management Supervise, guide, and coordinate the activities of QA/QC inspectors, technicians, and other assigned quality personnel. Allocate inspection duties and responsibilities based on production schedules and operational requirements. Monitor the performance, productivity, and effectiveness of quality assurance personnel. Provide technical guidance and training on quality inspection methods, printing defects, product specifications, and applicable quality standards. Ensure that quality personnel consistently follow established inspection procedures and reporting requirements. Promote teamwork, discipline, accountability, and a strong quality culture across the production operation. Identify staff training and development needs and recommend appropriate capacity-building interventions. Continuous Improvement and Quality Management Systems Identify opportunities to improve production quality, reduce material wastage, minimize rework, and prevent customer complaints. Monitor quality trends and recommend preventive measures to address recurring operational and product-related problems. Participate in continuous improvement initiatives, 5S activities, and other quality improvement programs. Support the development, implementation, maintenance, and continuous improvement of the company's Quality Management System. Monitor compliance with approved quality procedures, work instructions, and operational standards. Participate in internal quality audits and follow up on the implementation of audit findings and corrective actions. Recommend improvements to inspection methods, production processes, and quality control procedures to enhance operational efficiency. Customer and Supplier Quality Coordination Review customer specifications, product requirements, and special quality expectations to ensure their proper communication and implementation throughout production. Coordinate with Customer Service and Production teams to address customer quality concerns and ensure timely resolution of complaints. Support customer audits, quality inspections, and technical visits where required. Coordinate with Procurement, Warehouse, and Quality personnel to assess the conformity of incoming raw materials and production consumables. Provide feedback regarding supplier-related quality problems and support supplier performance evaluation. Communicate relevant quality requirements and material specifications to production personnel and other concerned stakeholders. Ensure that customer-specific quality requirements are properly documented and monitored throughout the production process. Performs other related duties as directed.",
